IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cdba-nouns`
IMPORT `cdba-calendar`

-- Canada Disability Benefit Regulations (SOR/2025-35), sections 10 and 11 -- SUSPENSION OF
-- PAYMENTS: by the Minister (s 10) and at the beneficiary's own request (s 11).
--
-- Every judgment the text hands to the Minister ("reasonable grounds to believe", "satisfied",
-- "a reasonable time") is a plain BOOLEAN input here, never worked out.
--
-- A suspension under s 10 does not make the beneficiary ineligible (s 2(6) names only s 11),
-- so months of a s 10 suspension keep their section 6 amounts, which s 10(3) pays on lifting.

§ `Regulations s 10 -- Potential ineligibility`

-- 10(1): the Minister may suspend payment if the Minister has reasonable grounds to believe
-- the beneficiary does not meet the criteria of section 2, or that an inquiry about their
-- eligibility is necessary.
-- src:148 | 10 (1) If the Minister has reasonable grounds to believe that a beneficiary does not meet the eligibility criteria set out in section 2 or that an inquiry with respect to their eligibility is necessary, the Minister may suspend payment of the allocation to the beneficiary until the Minister is satisfied that they are eligible.
@ref Regulations s 10(1) (src:148)
GIVEN `the Minister has reasonable grounds to believe that the beneficiary does not meet the eligibility criteria set out in section 2` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister has reasonable grounds to believe that an inquiry with respect to the beneficiary's eligibility is necessary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Minister may suspend payment of the allocation` `the Minister has reasonable grounds to believe that the beneficiary does not meet the eligibility criteria set out in section 2` `the Minister has reasonable grounds to believe that an inquiry with respect to the beneficiary's eligibility is necessary` MEANS
        `the Minister has reasonable grounds to believe that the beneficiary does not meet the eligibility criteria set out in section 2`
     OR `the Minister has reasonable grounds to believe that an inquiry with respect to the beneficiary's eligibility is necessary`

-- 10(1) "until the Minister is satisfied that they are eligible": the suspension may last
-- only while the Minister is not satisfied.
@ref Regulations s 10(1) (src:148)
GIVEN `the Minister is satisfied that the beneficiary is eligible` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Minister may keep payment of the allocation suspended` `the Minister is satisfied that the beneficiary is eligible` MEANS
    NOT `the Minister is satisfied that the beneficiary is eligible`

-- 10(2): the review must be within a reasonable time. Whether a reasonable time has passed
-- is the Minister's and ultimately a tribunal's judgment; it is an input. The text names no
-- consequence of a late review; the rule says only that the Minister's duty is unmet.
-- src:150 | (2) The Minister must review a beneficiary’s eligibility within a reasonable time.
@ref Regulations s 10(2) (src:150)
GIVEN `payment of the allocation is suspended under subsection 10(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a reasonable time has passed since the suspension began` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister has reviewed the beneficiary's eligibility` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Minister has not reviewed the beneficiary's eligibility within a reasonable time` `payment of the allocation is suspended under subsection 10(1)` `a reasonable time has passed since the suspension began` `the Minister has reviewed the beneficiary's eligibility` MEANS
        `payment of the allocation is suspended under subsection 10(1)`
    AND `a reasonable time has passed since the suspension began`
    AND NOT `the Minister has reviewed the beneficiary's eligibility`

-- 10(3): when the suspension is lifted the Minister must resume payment and pay a lump sum
-- equal to the sum of the payments, worked out under section 6, that the beneficiary was
-- entitled to receive during the suspension. The amounts are given one per month of the
-- suspension, with 0 for a month in which the beneficiary was not entitled.
-- src:152 | (3) If a suspension is lifted, the Minister must resume payment of the allocation and make a lump sum payment that is equal to the sum of the payments, as calculated in accordance with section 6, that the beneficiary was entitled to receive during the period of the suspension.
@ref Regulations s 10(3) (src:152)
GIVEN `the suspension has been lifted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Minister must resume payment and pay a lump sum` `the suspension has been lifted` MEANS
    `the suspension has been lifted`

@ref Regulations s 10(3) (src:152)
GIVEN `the amounts under section 6 for the months of the suspension` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lump sum on lifting a suspension` `the amounts under section 6 for the months of the suspension` MEANS
    sum `the amounts under section 6 for the months of the suspension`

§ `Regulations s 11 -- Request for suspension`

-- 11(1) and 11(2): a beneficiary may ask in writing; payment is suspended on the later of
-- the last day of the month in which the Minister processes the request and the day the
-- request names (if it names one). A request that is not in writing is not a request under
-- s 11(1): NOTHING.
-- src:154 | 11 (1) A beneficiary may request in writing that the Minister suspend payment of their allocation.
-- src:155 | Suspension of payments
-- src:156 | (2) The payment of an allocation is suspended on the later of
-- src:157 | (a) the last day of the month in which the request is processed by the Minister, and
-- src:158 | (b) the day indicated in the beneficiary’s request.
@ref Regulations s 11(1) and (2) (src:154-158)
GIVEN `the request is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the Minister processes the request` IS A DATE
      `the day indicated in the request` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the day on which payment of the allocation is suspended` `the request is in writing` `the day the Minister processes the request` `the day indicated in the request` MEANS
    IF `the request is in writing`
    THEN CONSIDER `the day indicated in the request`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST lastDay
         WHEN JUST indicated THEN JUST (`the later day of` lastDay indicated)
    ELSE NOTHING
    WHERE lastDay MEANS `the last day of the month of` `the day the Minister processes the request`

-- 11(3): a request to resume must be in writing and made within 24 months after the date of
-- suspension; if none is received in that period the allocation is deemed to have ceased and
-- a new application is needed. Whether the allocation "is deemed to have ceased" depends on
-- the day it is asked about.
-- src:160 | (3) The beneficiary may request in writing that the Minister resume payment of their allocation within 24 months after the date of suspension. If no request to resume payment is received within that period, the allocation is deemed to have ceased and they must make a new application for benefits to receive the allocation again.
@ref Regulations s 11(3) (src:160)
GIVEN `the day of the suspension` IS A DATE
      `the day the request to resume was received` IS A DATE
      `the request to resume is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a request to resume payment is made in time` `the day of the suspension` `the day the request to resume was received` `the request to resume is in writing` MEANS
        `the request to resume is in writing`
    AND `the day the request to resume was received` AT MOST `add months` `the day of the suspension` 24

@ref Regulations s 11(3) (src:160)
GIVEN `the day of the suspension` IS A DATE
      `the day a request to resume payment made in time was received` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the allocation is deemed to have ceased and a new application is needed` `the day of the suspension` `the day a request to resume payment made in time was received` `the day asked about` MEANS
        `the day asked about` GREATER THAN `add months` `the day of the suspension` 24
    AND (CONSIDER `the day a request to resume payment made in time was received`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
         WHEN JUST d  THEN FALSE)

-- 11(4): on receipt of a request to resume, the Minister must resume payment if satisfied
-- that the person meets the criteria of section 2.
-- src:162 | (4) On receipt of a request to resume payments, the Minister must resume payment of the allocation if the Minister is satisfied that the person meets the eligibility criteria set out in section 2.
@ref Regulations s 11(4) (src:162)
GIVEN `a request to resume payments has been received` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister is satisfied that the person meets the eligibility criteria set out in section 2` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Minister must resume payment of the allocation` `a request to resume payments has been received` `the Minister is satisfied that the person meets the eligibility criteria set out in section 2` MEANS
        `a request to resume payments has been received`
    AND `the Minister is satisfied that the person meets the eligibility criteria set out in section 2`

-- 11(5): payment resumes in the later of the month after the month the Minister received the
-- request and the month the request names (if it names one). The month is returned as its
-- first day.
-- src:164 | (5) The Minister must resume payment of the allocation on the later of
-- src:165 | (a) the month following the month in which the Minister received the request, and
-- src:166 | (b) the month indicated in the beneficiary’s request.
@ref Regulations s 11(5) (src:164-166)
GIVEN `the day the Minister received the request to resume` IS A DATE
      `a day in the month indicated in the request` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the month in which payment of the allocation resumes` `the day the Minister received the request to resume` `a day in the month indicated in the request` MEANS
    CONSIDER `a day in the month indicated in the request`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN following
    WHEN JUST indicated THEN `the later day of` following (`the first day of the month of` indicated)
    WHERE following MEANS `the first day of the month after the month of` `the day the Minister received the request to resume`
